 ## Overview
-This method is a hardware-accelerated pipeline stage that performs perspective projection, gradient estimation, and volume data resampling to generate ray starting points and sample values for volume rendering [S1]. It solves the bottleneck where software implementations spend approximately 80% of computation time on geometry operations, perspective calculations, and resampling [S1]. It is distinguished from general-purpose GPU ray casting by its dedicated, fixed-function hardware for backward-mapping interpolation and gradient estimation, specifically optimized for the VIRIM architecture [S1].
