 ## Background
-This method originates from the VIRIM (Virtual Reality in Medicine) project, developed at the University of Mannheim [S1]. It was designed to address the computational intensity of volume rendering geometry operations, which dominate software-based implementations [S1]. The architecture was later commercially distributed by Volume Graphics GmbH . It represents a shift towards specialized hardware (ASIC/FPGA-like) for the resampling stage, preceding modern GPU-based approaches by utilizing dedicated DSPs for the subsequent shading stage [S1].
